preConditionHook:
// EEC E18 "Where You At?" verbatim, deliberately NOT split: the book's
// time exclusion (time < 1600 or time > 2300) AND its 2-bar range-position
// test, with the book's literal .000001 epsilon. Equals TimeWindow(1600,
// 2300) negated + TwoBarRangePosition(0.5); kept whole to test the book's
// exact composite.
// EL Time is the bar's closing time as HHMM (EL_FEATURES.md `time`, VERIFIED:
// exchange clock, wall-clock close, no timezone conversion; a bar closing at
// midnight reads 0). ctx.Time(0) is that same close timestamp, so HHMM is its
// seconds-of-day re-packed -- the TimeOfDayExit derivation.
barSeconds = seconds_of_day(ctx.Time(0));
barHHMM = (barSeconds / 3600) * 100 + (barSeconds % 3600) / 60;
// EEC E18: ll = minlist(l, l[1]); hh = maxlist(h, h[1]) -- the book's spelling.
// MinList/MaxList are ACCEPTED for tick-grid PRICE operands only
// (EL_FEATURES.md): these operands differ by 0 or by >= 1 tick, ~1e9x the
// relational tolerance, so whichever comparison they carry cannot matter and
// the plain ternary stand-in is exact -- same arrangement as AtrProfitTarget's
// TrueRange. (<algorithm> is not among the emitted includes, so no std::min.)
ll = low[0] < low[1] ? low[0] : low[1];
hh = high[0] > high[1] ? high[0] : high[1];
